# Cursor Instructions — Parvati Climbing NGO (Next.js repo: `parvati-next`)

These instructions guide Cursor to continue development for the **Parvati Climbing NGO** website using the existing Next.js scaffold. Keep everything **CMS‑ready**, narrative‑driven, and aligned with the client's initial vision. primary KPI = awareness + storytelling impact

---

## 0) Project Context (from client meeting)
- **Hero**: Intro to **Mission + Vision**; highlight impact *through climbing*.
- **About**: Keep simple for v1 (history + people). **Theory of Change** section will be added later.
- **Partners/Collaborators**: Show key collaborators/partners.
- **Primary goal (v1)**: **General awareness** (not lead gen, not bookings yet).
- **Media**: Embed **Instagram posts** (in Contact/Media area).
- **Donate**: Button links **externally to GoFundMe** (no internal checkout for v1).
- **Theme**: Climbing‑centric visuals + **custom loader** tied to mountain climbing; tasteful **GSAP/Anime.js** narrative animations.
- **Sitemap (v1)**: **Home**, **About** (history + people), **Projects**, **Partners**, **Donate** (GoFundMe), **Contact Us** (includes Instagram).
- **CMS‑ready**: Code for future headless CMS (Strapi/Directus/Sanity), editable content schemas, no hardcoding copy.
- **Hosting**: Keep deployable (e.g., Vercel/HF Space/GitHub Pages).

> Non‑goals (for v1): program bookings, lead capture, forms beyond basic contact, complex e‑commerce.

---

## 1) Tech & Conventions
- **Framework**: Next.js (App Router not required; Pages Router OK as scaffolded).
- **Styling**: Global CSS (already present). Keep components self‑contained; prefer CSS modules later if needed.
- **Animation**: **GSAP** (+ ScrollTrigger) for scroll orchestration; **Anime.js** for micro‑interactions.
- **Images**: Use `/public/assets` with responsive attributes; later switch to `next/image` as needed.
- **CMS‑ready**: Abstract content into `lib/mock/*.ts` (mock data) with interfaces matching planned schemas; in v2 swap to API calls.
- **Accessibility**: Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`; alt text required; keyboard focus states.
- **Performance**: Only animate opacity/transform; lazy‑load below‑the‑fold media.

---

## 2) Tasks — V1 Milestone (Awareness‑first)
> Target branch: `v1/awareness-draft`

### 2.1 Pages (routes)
- `/` **Home**: narrative hero, program highlights, project teaser, partner strip, donate CTA.
- `/about` **About**: short history + team (people grid). Placeholder slot for "Theory of Change" (hidden until content exists).
- `/projects` **Projects**: list of projects (cards) with location tag (Jamaica/Parvati/etc.), short description, gallery placeholder.
- `/partners` **Partners**: grid of collaborator logos with links; short descriptions.
- `/donate` **Donate**: brief rationale + **GoFundMe external link** (primary CTA).
- `/contact` **Contact**: email, location, and **Instagram embed** (posts/carousel).

### 2.2 Navigation & Footer
- Update primary nav to: Home, About, Projects, Partners, Donate, Contact.
- Footer with address/email, Instagram link, and small print.

### 2.3 Narrative & Motion
- **Hero rope path** draws on mount; CTA "clip" micro‑motion (carabiner).
- **Scroll reveals** for sections (staggered cards, soft parallax).
- **Reduced motion** guard: fallback to non‑animated static reveals.
- **Custom loader**: a minimalist climber/carabiner loop Lottie or CSS/GIF (swap in later with asset).

### 2.4 Content & Mock Data
Create `lib/mock/` with:
- `site.ts` — site meta, nav, footer, social (instagram handle/url).  
- `team.ts` — `{ name, role, headshot, bioShort }[]`  
- `projects.ts` — `{ title, region, excerpt, images[], status }[]`  
- `partners.ts` — `{ name, logo, url, blurb }[]`  

> Wire pages to read from `lib/mock/*` so copy is not hardcoded. Use placeholders now; later replace with CMS API.

### 2.5 Components (minimum set)
- `components/Nav.tsx`
- `components/Hero.tsx` *(rope path + CTA)*
- `components/StripPartners.tsx` *(logo strip with subtle motion)*
- `components/ProjectCards.tsx` *(grid + reveal)*
- `components/TeamGrid.tsx`
- `components/InstagramEmbed.tsx` *(simple iframe/embed)*

Keep component APIs **data‑driven** (accept props typed by mock interfaces).

### 2.6 Donate Flow (external)
- `/donate` page: one primary button → **GoFundMe link** (target=`_blank`, `rel="noopener noreferrer"`).

### 2.7 Accessibility & SEO
- Page titles/meta for each route.
- Landmark tags (`<header>`, `<main>`, `<footer>`).
- Alt text required for images (lint if possible).
- Google Analytics/Meta Pixel integration for awareness tracking

