## 6) Development Guidelines & Restrictions

### Code Quality Standards
- Write clean, self-documenting code with meaningful variable and function names
- Add comments for complex logic or business rules
- Follow React hooks rules and best practices
- Implement proper error handling and loading states
- Ensure responsive design across all screen sizes
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion` for accessibility

### Code Restrictions
- **NO** direct DOM manipulation - use React state and props
- **NO** inline styles unless absolutely necessary - prefer CSS classes
- **NO** hardcoded content values - use `lib/mock/*` data files
- **NO** console.log statements in production code
- **NO** unused imports or variables
- **NO** overly complex components - break them down into smaller ones

### File and Directory Structure
- Follow Next.js file-based routing conventions (Pages Router)
- Keep components modular in `/components` directory
- Store mock data in `/lib/mock/` directory
- Store types/interfaces in `/types/` directory
- Place static assets in `/public/assets`
- Use consistent naming conventions (PascalCase for components, camelCase for functions/variables)

### Animation Guidelines
- Use GSAP for scroll orchestration and complex animations
- Use Anime.js for micro-interactions and simple animations
- Only animate opacity/transform properties for performance
- Always provide fallbacks for `prefers-reduced-motion`
- Lazy-load below-the-fold animations

### CMS-Ready Development
- Abstract all content into mock data files
- Create typed interfaces for all content schemas
- Wire components to accept data via props
- Prepare for future API integration
- Avoid hardcoded copy in components

